@EricEzaM Is this still an issue for you? @golddotasksquestions, in his edited comment, says _"On the joy axis the triggers work fine, deadzone included."_ with a Xbox One Controller. I have now tested this on Windows with a PS3 controller and it (including the dead zone) works fine for me too.

The only thing I can think of is the Action Deadzone, which despite you saying _"I have the deadzone set to 0% here"_, in your MRP it is set to the default 50%; so the behaviour you're seeing would be expected.

BTW See https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/3709 for a proposal on making the axes dead zone configurable and changing the default to a more reasonable value of 5%.
